CREATED:20260412T212937Z
DESCRIPTION:All Duke students are invited to attend an information session
  about a unique Duke practicum course that examines the negotiation of in
 ternational climate change agreements under the United Nations Framework 
 Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC).\n\nFeatured speakers will include 
 Jackson Ewing (Nicholas Institute expert and practicum faculty sponsor) a
 nd Gabriela Nagle Alverio (Duke J.D. - Ph.D. and former practicum teachin
 g assistant).\n\nIn the past\, practicum students have had the opportunit
 y to attend the annual international negotiations. Participants in the fa
 ll 2026 course may be able to travel to the 31st Conference of the Partie
 s (COP 31) in in Antalya\, Türkiye\; the opportunity for course travel is
  subject to change based on Duke's international travel policies and indi
 vidual visa restrictions.\n\nDuke students from all fields\, departments\
 , and programs (including upper-level undergraduate students and those in
  masters\, professional\, and doctoral degree programs) are encouraged to
  apply to take part in the practicum\; the only prerequisite is a passion
  for climate change policy.\n\nInterested students should join the Nichol
 as Institute email list for updates on the process and register for the Z
 oom info session on April 23 at 12 - 1 p.m. ET. Applications will be rele
 ased later this summer and more information on the application process wi
 ll be discussed in the info session.\n\nQuestions? Reach out to Colleen N
 ieto at colleen.nieto@duke.edu\n\nNOTE: This info session is only for cur
 rent Duke students.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260414T143647Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260423T120000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260414T143647Z
