CREATED:20260317T225929Z
DESCRIPTION:Shift your perspective. \n\nJoin the Duke Center for Documenta
 ry Studies (CDS) for our annual celebration of student documentary work a
 nd new creative visions!\n \n->| Explore exhibitions featuring work from 
 CDS undergraduate courses. \n\n-->| Meet students graduating from our Und
 ergraduate Education and from our Continuing Education programs.\n\n--->|
  Enjoy live music by Little Chair (an all-Duke student band) and free foo
 d from the Boricua Soul food truck. \n\n---->| Enter a raffle for a bundl
 e of CDS photo books (must be present at drawing at 6:00 p.m. to win). \n
 \n"Shifts: New Expressions 2026" is an ongoing exhibit - student work ins
 talled in April will be on view into the summer\, so you can keep coming 
 back to take it all in.\n\nFree and open to all - students\, faculty\, st
 aff\, and community members.\n\nPROGRAM\n\n5:00 p.m. | Doors open\, exhib
 itions on view\, raffle & free food tickets available (while supplies las
 t) \n5:15 p.m. | Live music starts \n6:00 p.m. | Welcome\, raffle drawing
 \, & presentation of Undergraduate Certificates \n6:15 p.m. | Remarks & p
 resentation of Continuing Education Certificates\n6:30 p.m. | Presentatio
 n & film screening (Elizabeth M. Webb\, 2024-2026 Lehman Brady Visiting J
 oint Chair Professor)\n\nImage: Dhruv Rungta
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20260414T132801Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260423T170000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260414T132801Z
